{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Separation of Concerns.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Separation of Concerns.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"separation of concerns separation of concerns","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Separation of Concerns.md","fileName":"Separation of Concerns.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Separation of Concerns","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:37\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Front-End Service Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Front-End Service Design","Entity Framework Core Entity","Data Transfer Object","Angular Service","Angular Component","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Separation of Concerns.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Separation of Concerns.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"separation of concerns separation of concerns","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Separation of Concerns.md","fileName":"Separation of Concerns.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Separation of Concerns","heading":"Separation of Concerns","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Separation of concerns assigns different responsibilities to different parts of a system so each can change without carrying unrelated duties. A full-stack application separates persistence entities, API output, client communication, and presentation even when their data initially looks similar.\n\nAn [[Entity Framework Core Entity]] should model stored state, while a [[Data Transfer Object]] exposes the controlled shape needed by the client. An [[Angular Service]] handles reusable communication so an [[Angular Component]] can focus on interface state.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Front-End Service Design","Entity Framework Core Entity","Data Transfer Object","Angular Service","Angular Component","aspnetcore3anda